ROADMAP.md:158:| B. Cumulative slices 0 and 1, then LP0 | Slice 0 establishes the running proof infrastructure: a closed `u8` arithmetic subset through every used IR to two unverified native builds, with per-lowering proofs and the composed conditional theorem. Then `ConcreteSpec` and the new compiler for slice 1 (the approved linear component, row Q8.2), on the same path; then LP0. See [vertical slices](#vertical-slices). | Each slice meets the [slice shape](#vertical-slices). Every judgment, semantics and pass is total. Fuel exhaustion is distinct from divergence. The native builds are qualified by tests, not proved: the LLVM output is labelled unverified, and its assumptions are listed with the lexer, model-translation and native-image obligations; a native-image claim, if any, is stated separately as conditional on those assumptions. Minimal provenance accompanies the first authoritative proof claims. The outside-reader test passes on the Lean rules. Phase B closes after slice 1, LP0 and B2/B3 acceptance; `legacy/` stays until LD. |
ROADMAP.md:159:| C. File-copy | Workloads grow from simple proved examples to file-copy and then supported real programs; each records program correctness, authority, failure behaviour and residual assumptions. [Vertical slices](#vertical-slices) 2 to 18, each meeting the slice shape: integers, control flow, loops, functions, authority, secrets, the proof surface, structs, enums, generics, `Option`/`Result`, references, traits and `defer`, arrays, text and the console, modules, and files, ending at file-copy. Std, examples and tests come back as their constructs land. | The file-copy program, failure paths included, builds natively with its theorems. **0.1 is cut** at slice 18 with the supported subset, the unsupported constructs, the LLVM assumptions and the proven zero-heap facts stated. |
ROADMAP.md:160:| D. Whole language | [Vertical slices](#vertical-slices) 19 to 28: allocation, function values, heap arrays, `Vec` and `String`, maps, raw pointers, FFI (then RocksDB slice 1), floats, clock, network and devices, and concurrency as the final slice (then ethlambda and the encrypted tunnel). | Every construct of the decided language is a slice with Lean rules, and the conformance suite is complete. |
ROADMAP.md:161:| E. Verified growth | Proof-order items 4–8, the Lean Compiler Backend native path, the verified parser, typed contracts, frame reasoning, termination proofs and the proof library. Earlier slices already contain example-specific program theorems; E expands reusable models and proof support. Contracts have no source `old` and no snapshot construct (OD117): a postcondition reaches the entry state only through an explicit Lean theorem. Spec functions are total (OD115). An ordinary function can get its own termination proof, and there is no total-function category (OD116). | Each item's theorem holds, with its residual assumptions stated. |
ROADMAP.md:168:**Active:** A2i (integrating the proposed spec), B0 (the slice-0 design is done; building it is next) and folding the decided diagnostics, memory and information-flow interfaces into A2i (R-0592). What waits for the owner is [listed in the decisions](docs/decisions.md#waiting-for-the-owner). **Next:** A2c (the owner's spec read and freeze), then B1. The legacy move (T0–T2) has landed; A1 and A2b feed A2i. A2a (provisional approval of the Core shape, decision row Q9.19) is done: the owner approved every Core row on 2026-11-05 ([record](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05)); the approval binds the design without freezing it.
