ROADMAP.md:177:| A2i | Integrate the proposed spec before the freeze ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06)) | R-0571, R-0574, R-0496, R-0560, R-0555, R-0559, R-0588, R-0592, R-0602, R-0603, R-0607, R-0608, R-0609, R-0610, R-0611, R-0612, R-0613, R-0614, R-0615, R-0616 | The shared foundation, contracts C1–C10 ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-08-foundation)), is written in Lean with its laws proved, before slice 1 builds on it; each later slice adds its rules without rewriting it ([foundation first](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-foundation-first)). The separately proved parts share Core interfaces and one integrated semantics. Interaction proofs hold for a borrow across deferred cleanup, an allocator reset with outstanding loans and cleanup that needs authority, and the README obligations [O7 and O9](ConcreteSpec/README.md) are discharged. The semantic contract is stated. The normative definitions are one library in cohesive modules with `Spec.lean` as the public import. The browsable owner view exists. The pre-freeze part of R-0574 (no hidden traps and bounded execution) is in the proposed spec. An outside reader has read the integrated spec through that view. |
ROADMAP.md:181:| B1 | Build `ConcreteSpec` and slice 1 with its theorem | R-0425, R-0499, R-0492, R-0493, R-0514, R-0501, R-0503, R-0497, R-0504, R-0507, R-0521, R-0552, R-0528, R-0479, R-0118, R-0573, R-0576, R-0577, R-0579, R-0580, R-0582, R-0586, R-0588, R-0589, R-0599, R-0600 | [Slice 1](#vertical-slices) meets the slice shape: it runs from parsing to both native builds, its judgments are independent, its correspondence and soundness are proved, its obligations are explicit and its provenance is minimal. |
