ROADMAP.md:324:- **grep at 18: command-line input gap.** The adopted `grep PATTERN FILE` stage needs argument access (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), but args/cli are not placed. The legacy accessor returns an allocating String (`legacy/std/src/args.con` line 22); legacy CLI stores Vec/String (`legacy/std/src/cli.con` line 27, `legacy/std/src/cli.con` line 50). Allocation arrives at 19 and Vec/String at 22 (slices 19 and 22 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)), after zero-heap slice 18 (slice 18 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). A nonallocating argument contract is unresolved; this table does not choose one. The same gap applies to the file encryptor at 18 if it takes command-line paths, which its adopted row does not specify.
ROADMAP.md:328:- **Wide-integer arithmetic is unplaced.** EVM 15 needs u256 arithmetic and X25519 and Poly1305 at 15/18 need arithmetic wider than u64 (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)); the integer types stop at 64 bits and no limb or wide-integer module is placed, so these stages have no module contract yet.
